#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:1
msgid "Release 2.34.0 (2026-02-27)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:3
msgid "Highlights"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:5
msgid "Rust nix-installer in beta"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:7
msgid ""
"The Rust-based rewrite of the Nix installer is now in beta. We'd love help "
"testing it out!"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:10
msgid "To test out the new installer, run:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:11
msgid ""
"```\n"
"curl -sSfL https://artifacts.nixos.org/nix-installer | sh -s -- install\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:15
msgid ""
"This installer can be run even when you have an existing, script-based Nix "
"installation without any adjustments."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:17
msgid ""
"This new installer also comes with the ability to uninstall your Nix "
"installation; run:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:22
msgid ""
"This will get rid of your entire Nix installation (even if you installed "
"over an existing, script-based installation)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:24
msgid ""
"This installer is a modified version of the [Determinate Nix Installer]"
"(https://github.com/DeterminateSystems/nix-installer) by Determinate "
"Systems. Thanks to Determinate Systems for all the investment they've put "
"into the installer."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:27
msgid ""
"Source for the installer is in <https://github.com/NixOS/nix-installer>. "
"Report any issues in that repo."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:30
msgid ""
"For CI usage, a GitHub Action to install Nix using this installer is "
"available at <https://github.com/NixOS/nix-installer-action>."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:32
msgid ""
"Stabilisation of `no-url-literals` experimental feature and new diagnostics "
"infrastructure, with `lint-url-literals`, `lint-short-path-literals`, and "
"`lint-absolute-path-literals` settings [\\#8738](https://github.com/NixOS/"
"nix/issues/8738) [\\#10048](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/10048) "
"[\\#10281](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/10281) [\\#15326](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15326)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:34
msgid ""
"Experimental feature `no-url-literals` has been stabilised and is now "
"controlled by the `lint-url-literals` option. New diagnostics infrastructure "
"has been added for linting discouraged language features."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:37
msgid "New lint infrastructure"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:39
msgid ""
"[`lint-url-literals`](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-lint-url-literals)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:41
msgid ""
"The `no-url-literals` experimental feature has been stabilised and replaced "
"with a new [`lint-url-literals`](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-lint-url-"
"literals) setting."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:43
msgid "To migrate from the experimental feature, replace:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:47 source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:60
msgid "with:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:52
msgid ""
"[`lint-short-path-literals`](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-lint-short-"
"path-literals)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:54
msgid ""
"The [`warn-short-path-literals`](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-warn-short-"
"path-literals) boolean setting has been deprecated and replaced with [`lint-"
"short-path-literals`](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-lint-short-path-"
"literals)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:56
msgid "To migrate, replace:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:65
msgid ""
"[`lint-absolute-path-literals`](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-lint-"
"absolute-path-literals)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:67
msgid ""
"A new [`lint-absolute-path-literals`](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-lint-"
"absolute-path-literals) setting has been added to control handling of "
"absolute path literals (paths starting with `/`) and home path literals "
"(paths starting with `~/`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:69
msgid "Setting values"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:71
msgid "All three settings accept three values:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:72
msgid "`ignore`: Allow the feature without emitting any diagnostic (default)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:73
msgid "`warn`: Emit a warning when the feature is used"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:74
msgid "`fatal`: Treat the feature as a parse error"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:76
msgid "The defaults may change in future versions."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:78
msgid ""
"Improved parser error messages [\\#15092](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/15092)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:80
msgid ""
"Parser error messages now use legible strings for tokens instead of internal "
"names. For example, malformed expression `a ++ ++ b` now produces the "
"following error:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:88
msgid "Instead of:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:96
msgid "New features"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:98
msgid ""
"`nix repl` now supports `inherit` and multiple bindings [\\#15082](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15082)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:100
msgid ""
"The `nix repl` now supports `inherit` statements and multiple bindings per "
"line:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:117
msgid ""
"New command `nix store roots-daemon` for serving GC roots [\\#15143](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15143)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:119
msgid ""
"New command [`nix store roots-daemon`](../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-"
"roots-daemon.md) runs a daemon that serves garbage collector roots over a "
"Unix domain socket. It enables the garbage collector to discover runtime "
"roots when the main Nix daemon doesn't have `CAP_SYS_PTRACE` capability and "
"therefore cannot scan `/proc`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:122
msgid ""
"The garbage collector can be configured to use this daemon via the [`use-"
"roots-daemon`](../store/types/local-store.md#store-local-store-use-roots-"
"daemon) store setting."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:124
msgid ""
"This feature requires the [`local-overlay-store` experimental feature](../"
"development/experimental-features.md#xp-feature-local-overlay-store)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:126
msgid ""
"New command `nix-nswrapper` in `libexec` [\\#15183](https://github.com/NixOS/"
"nix/pull/15183)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:128
msgid ""
"The new command `libexec/nix-nswrapper` is used to run the Nix daemon in an "
"unprivileged user namespace on Linux. In order to use this command, build "
"user UIDs and GIDs must be allocated in `/etc/subuid` and `/etc/subgid`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:130
msgid ""
"It can be used to run the Nix daemon with full sandboxing without executing "
"as root. Support has been added to Nixpkgs with the new `nix.daemonUser` and "
"`nix.daemonGroup` settings."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:132
msgid ""
"New setting `ignore-gc-delete-failure` for local stores [\\#15054](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15054)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:134
msgid ""
"A new local store setting [`ignore-gc-delete-failure`](../store/types/local-"
"store.md#store-local-store-ignore-gc-delete-failure) has been added. When "
"enabled, garbage collection will log warnings instead of failing when it "
"cannot delete store paths. This is useful when running Nix as an "
"unprivileged user that may not have write access to all paths in the store."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:138
msgid ""
"This setting is experimental and requires the [`local-overlay-store`](../"
"development/experimental-features.md#xp-feature-local-overlay-store) "
"experimental feature."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:140
msgid ""
"New setting `narinfo-cache-meta-ttl` [\\#15287](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/15287)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:142
msgid ""
"The new setting `narinfo-cache-meta-ttl` controls how long binary cache "
"metadata (i.e. `/nix-cache-info`) is cached locally, in seconds. This was "
"previously hard-coded to 7 days, which is still the default. As a result, "
"you can now use `nix store info --refresh` to check whether a binary cache "
"is still valid."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:144
msgid ""
"Support HTTPS binary caches using mTLS (client certificate) authentication "
"[\\#13002](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/13002) [\\#13030](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/13030)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:146
msgid ""
"Added support for `tls-certificate` and `tls-private-key` options in "
"substituter URLs."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:148
msgid "Example:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:150
msgid ""
"```\n"
"https://substituter.invalid?tls-certificate=/path/to/cert.pem&tls-private-"
"key=/path/to/key.pem\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:154
msgid ""
"When these options are configured, Nix will use this certificate/private key "
"pair to authenticate to the server."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:156
msgid ""
"`nix store gc --dry-run` and `nix-collect-garbage --dry-run` now report the "
"number of paths that would be freed [\\#15229](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/15229) [\\#5704](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/5704)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:158
msgid "Performance improvements"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:160
msgid ""
"Unpacking tarballs to `~/.cache/nix/tarball-cache-v2` is now multithreaded "
"[\\#12087](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/12087)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:162
msgid ""
"Content-addressed cache for `builtins.fetchTarball` and tarball-based flake "
"inputs (e.g. `github:NixOS/nixpkgs`, `https://channels.nixos.org/nixos-25.11/"
"nixexprs.tar.xz`) now writes git blobs (files) to the `tarball-cache-v2` "
"repository concurrently, which significantly reduces the wall time for "
"tarball unpacking (up to ~1.8x faster unpacking for `https://channels.nixos."
"org/nixos-25.11/nixexprs.tar.xz` in our testing)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:164
msgid ""
"Currently, Nix doesn't perform any maintenance on the `~/.cache/nix/tarball-"
"cache-v2` repository, which will be addressed in future versions. Users that "
"wish to reclaim disk space used by the tarball cache may want to run:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:171
msgid ""
"`nix nar ls` and other NAR listing operations have been optimised further "
"[\\#15163](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15163)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:173
msgid ""
"Evaluator hot-path optimizations [\\#15270](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/15270) [\\#15271](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15271)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:175
msgid "C API Changes"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:177
msgid ""
"New store API methods [\\#14766](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/14766) "
"[\\#14768](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/14768)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:179
msgid "The C API now includes additional methods:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:181
msgid ""
"`nix_store_query_path_from_hash_part()` - Get the full store path given its "
"hash part"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:182
msgid ""
"`nix_store_copy_path()` - Copy a single store path between two stores, "
"allows repairs and configuring signature checking"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:184
msgid ""
"Errors returned from your primops are not treated as recoverable by default "
"[\\#13930](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/13930) [\\#15286](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15286)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:186
msgid "Nix 2.34 by default remembers the error in the thunk that triggered it."
msgstr ""

