msgid "**Resolution**"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:198
msgid ""
"C API consumers that rely on this must change their recoverable error calls:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:205
msgid "Bug fixes"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:207
msgid ""
"Avoid dropping ssh connections with `ssh-ng://` stores for store path "
"copying [\\#14998](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/14998) [\\#6950]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/6950)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:209
msgid ""
"Due to a bug in how Nix handled Boost.Coroutine2 suspension and resumption, "
"copying from `ssh-ng://` stores would drop the SSH connection for each "
"copied path. This issue has been fixed, which improves performance by "
"avoiding multiple SSH/Nix Worker Protocol handshakes."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:211
msgid ""
"S3 binary caches now use virtual-hosted-style addressing by default "
"[\\#15208](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/15208) [\\#15216](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15216)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:213
msgid ""
"S3 binary caches now use virtual-hosted-style URLs (`https://bucket.s3."
"region.amazonaws.com/key`) instead of path-style URLs (`https://s3.region."
"amazonaws.com/bucket/key`) when connecting to standard AWS S3 endpoints. "
"This enables HTTP/2 multiplexing and fixes TCP connection exhaustion "
"(TIME_WAIT socket accumulation) under high-concurrency workloads."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:219
msgid "A new `addressing-style` store option controls this behavior:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:221
msgid ""
"`auto` (default): virtual-hosted-style for standard AWS endpoints, path-"
"style for custom endpoints."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:223
msgid "`path`: forces path-style addressing (deprecated by AWS)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:224
msgid ""
"`virtual`: forces virtual-hosted-style addressing (bucket names must not "
"contain dots)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:227
msgid ""
"Bucket names containing dots (e.g., `my.bucket.name`) automatically fall "
"back to path-style addressing in `auto` mode, because dotted names create "
"multi-level subdomains that break TLS wildcard certificate validation."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:231
msgid "Example using path-style for backwards compatibility:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:233
msgid ""
"```\n"
"s3://my-bucket/key?region=us-east-1&addressing-style=path\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:237
msgid ""
"Additionally, TCP keep-alive is now enabled on all HTTP connections, "
"preventing idle connections from being silently dropped by intermediate "
"network devices (NATs, firewalls, load balancers)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:241
msgid ""
"`nix-prefetch-url --unpack` now properly checks for empty archives [\\#15242]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15242)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:243
msgid ""
"Prior versions failed to check for empty archives and would crash with a "
"`nullptr` dereference when unpacking empty archives. This is now fixed."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:246
msgid ""
"Prevent runaway processes when Nix is killed with `SIGKILL` when building in "
"a local store with build users [\\#15193](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/15193)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:248
msgid ""
"When run as root, Nix doesn't run builds via the daemon and is a parent of "
"the forked build processes. Prior versions of Nix failed to preserve the "
"`PR_SET_PDEATHSIG` parent-death signal across `setuid` calls. This could "
"lead to build processes being reparented and continue running in the "
"background. This has been fixed."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:250
msgid ""
"Fix crash when interrupting `--log-format internal-json` [\\#15335](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15335)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:252
msgid ""
"Pressing Ctrl-C during `--log-format internal-json` (used by [nix-output-"
"monitor](https://github.com/maralorn/nix-output-monitor)) no longer causes a "
"spurious \"Nix crashed. This is a bug.\" report."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:254
msgid ""
"Fix percent-encoding in `file://` and `local://` store URIs [\\#15280]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15280)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:256
msgid ""
"Store URIs with special characters like `+` in the path (e.g. `file:///tmp/"
"a+b`) no longer incorrectly create percent-encoded directories (e.g. `/tmp/"
"a%2Bb`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:258
msgid ""
"Fix crash during tab completion in `nix repl` [\\#15255](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/15255)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:260
msgid ""
"Fix \"Too many open files\" on macOS [\\#15205](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/15205)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:262
msgid ""
"Nix now raises the open file soft limit to the hard limit at startup, fixing "
"\"Too many open files\" errors on macOS where the default soft limit is low."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:264
msgid ""
"`nix develop` no longer fails when `inputs.nixpkgs` has `flake = false` "
"[\\#15175](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15175)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:266
msgid ""
"`builtins.flakeRefToString` no longer fails with \"attribute is a "
"thunk\" [\\#15160](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15160)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:268
msgid ""
"Fix `QueryPathInfo` throwing on invalid paths in the daemon [\\#15134]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15134)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:270
msgid ""
"`nix-store --generate-binary-cache-key` now fsyncs key files to prevent "
"corruption [\\#15107](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15107)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:272
msgid ""
"Fix `build-hook` setting in `nix.conf` being ignored [\\#15083](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15083)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:274
msgid ""
"Fix empty error messages when builds are cancelled due to a dependency "
"failure [\\#14972](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/14972)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:276
msgid ""
"When a build fails without `--keep-going`, other in-progress builds are "
"cancelled. Previously, these cancelled builds were incorrectly reported as "
"failed with empty error messages. This affected `buildPathsWithResults` "
"callers such as `nix flake check`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:278
msgid "Miscellaneous changes"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:280
msgid ""
"Content-Encoding decompression is now handled by libcurl [\\#14324](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/14324) [\\#15336](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/15336)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:282
msgid ""
"Transparent decompression of HTTP downloads specifying `Content-Encoding` "
"header now uses libcurl. This adds support for previously advertised, but "
"not supported `deflate` encoding as well as deprecated `x-gzip` alias. Non-"
"standard `xz`, `bzip2` encodings that were previously advertised are no "
"longer supported, as they do not commonly appear in the wild and should not "
"be sent by compliant servers."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:285
msgid ""
"`br`, `zstd`, `gzip` continue to be supported. Distro packaging should "
"ensure that the `libcurl` dependency is linked against required libraries to "
"support these encodings. By default, the build system now requires libcurl "
">= 8.17.0, which is not known to have issues around [pausing and "
"decompression](https://github.com/curl/curl/issues/16280)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:287
msgid ""
"Static builds now support S3 features (`libstore:s3-aws-auth` meson option) "
"[\\#15076](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15076)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:289
msgid ""
"Improved package-related error messages [\\#15349](https://github.com/NixOS/"
"nix/pull/15349)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:291
msgid ""
"Store path context is now rendered in the user-facing `hash^out` format "
"instead of the internal `!out!hash` format. A misleading error message in "
"`nix-env` that incorrectly blamed content-addressed derivations has been "
"fixed."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:294
msgid ""
"Improved error message for empty derivation files [\\#15298](https://github."
"com/NixOS/nix/pull/15298)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:296
msgid ""
"Parsing an empty `.drv` file (e.g. due to store corruption after an unclean "
"shutdown) now produces a clear error message instead of the cryptic "
"`expected string 'D'`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:298
msgid ""
"Relative `file:` paths for tarballs are now rejected with a clear error "
"[\\#14983](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/14983)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:300
msgid ""
"Continued progress on the Windows port, including build fixes, CI "
"improvements, and platform abstractions."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:302
msgid ""
"Nix docker images are now uploaded to [GHCR](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pkgs/container/nix) as part of the release process"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.34.md:304
msgid ""
"Historically, only pre-release builds of `amd64` docker images have been "
"uploaded to ghcr.io with the `latest` tag pointing to the last built image "
"from `master` branch. This has been fixed and going forward, <https://github."
"com/NixOS/nix/pkgs/container/nix> will include the same images as <https://"
"hub.docker.com/r/nixos/nix/> that are built by [Hydra](https://hydra.nixos."
"org/project/nix) for [arm64](https://hydra.nixos.org/job/nix/"
"maintenance-2.34/dockerImage.aarch64-linux) and [amd64](https://hydra.nixos."
"org/job/nix/maintenance-2.34/dockerImage.x86_64-linux). Pre-release versions "
"are no longer pushed to the registry."
msgstr ""

